ORDINANCE - Approving and establishing revised water and sewer rates, tap and system
development fees, administrative fees, service charges and penalties and septic and commercial waste
dump rates, as recommended by the Board of Public Utilities -- referred to Finance Committee (sponsor
-- Mr. Brown).
ORDINANCE - Amending the City of Cheyenne’s Sanitation Fee Schedule -- referred to
Finance Committee (sponsor -- Mr. Brown).
ORDINANCE - Appropriating moneys for the City of Cheyenne, Wyoming for the various
purposes in conducting the municipal government of said City and fixing the amount of general and
special taxes as part of the revenue required to meet the said appropriation, all for the Fiscal Year
beginning July 1, 2013, and ending June 30, 2014 -- referred to Committee of the Whole (sponsor --
Mr. Brown).
ORDINANCE - Pursuant to Section 2.2.1, Zoning Map Amendment, Section 5.1.2, Zoning
Districts Established, and Section 5.1.3, Official Zoning Map, of the Cheyenne Unified Development
Code, changing the zoning classification from MR-2 Medium Density Residential - Developing District
to NR-3 Neighborhood Residential - High Density District for Lot 14, Block 1, Saddle Ridge, Fifth
Filing, Cheyenne, Wyoming (located at the southwest corner of the intersection of Countryside Avenue
and Medicine Man Trail) -- referred to Public Services Committee (sponsor -- Mr. Allen).
ORDINANCE - Amending various Sections of Title 8, Health and Safety, Chapter 8.08, Alarm
Systems, of the Cheyenne City Code pertaining to Alarm Devices and Systems, and False Alarms --
referred to Finance Committee (sponsors -- Mr. Allen, Mr. Brown, Ms. Broyles, Mr. Cook, Mr. Luna,
Mr. Valdez and Ms. Williams).
ORDINANCE - Granting a Franchise by the City of Cheyenne to Cheyenne Light, Fuel and
Power Company, its successors and assigns, the right to furnish, sell and distribute natural gas to the
City and to all persons, businesses, and industry within a portion of the City in Cheyenne Light, Fuel
and Power Company’s Certificated Territory and the right to acquire, construct, install, locate, maintain,
operate and extend into, within and through said City all facilities reasonably necessary to furnish, sell
and distribute natural gas within the City and the right to make reasonable use of all streets and other
public places and public easements as herein defined as may be necessary; and fixing the terms and
conditions thereof -- referred to Finance Committee (sponsor - Mr. Brown).
[CA]
RESOLUTION - Approving the Title VI Program for the Cheyenne Transit Program, Cheyenne,
Wyoming, and the Cheyenne Metropolitan Planning Organization.  Motion (per Consent Agenda)
carried. (#5492)
[CA]
RESOLUTION - Authorizing submission of an application to the Wyoming Department of
Transportation for a Wyoming Rural Public Transportation Program Grant, for the purpose of assisting
in providing the local match for operating funds for the City of Cheyenne for its Transit Program, as
authorized by 49 U.S.C. § 5311 -- referred to Finance Committee (sponsor -- Mr. Brown).
